WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:05.250
A fork bomb replicates itself, without
stopping.

2
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:10.800
No privilege is needed, so even a hardened
system is exposed.

3
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:16.000
The process table fills, and the machine stops
answering.

4
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:20.030
Every usual defence breaks something else.

5
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.540
A process calls fork.

6
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.960
Its name is on the exception list.

7
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.140
So it is trusted, and runs unchecked.

8
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.920
Now something the system has never seen.

9
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.960
Not on the exception list.

10
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.730
And not a known offender.

11
00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.750
So its forks are counted.

12
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:50.690
Five hundred and twelve. Past the threshold.

13
00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:54.040
Killed, and the name recorded.

14
00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.970
The same name comes back.

15
00:00:57.470 --> 00:01:01.850
This time it is not killed. It runs capped.

16
00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.600
And watched. It keeps forking abnormally.

17
00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.020
So it is killed, before the table ever filled.

18
00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.560
Later, a legitimate program shares that name.

19
00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:21.100
Quarantined too. Suspected, not condemned.

20
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.240
Its fork rate stays normal.

21
00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.170
So the name is struck off.

22
00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:32.840
It forks freely. The false positive corrected
itself.

23
00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:38.560
Forty-four milliseconds, at a five hundred
fork threshold.

